    cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:dist-t-compare .
  ex:p1-n63-v rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:p1-pearson-contributions .
  ex:rv-f-v rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:dist-f .
  ex:rv-log-v rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:p1-log-transform .
  ex:rv-n14 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-normal ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:normal-measurement-model ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:nn-cdf-f ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:nn-cdf-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-normal-v ;
    cd:narration "For the Normal model, the CDF is written uppercase Phi and the density lowercase phi. At 10.20 mg/L, z = 2 gives cumulative probability 0.977249868 and upper-tail probability 0.022750132.\n\nIntegrating phi from minus infinity gives Phi. Its antiderivative uses the error function erf, with the scaling and half-offset shown in the formula."@en .
  ex:rv-n15 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-normal ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:normal-measurement-model ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:nn-tail-f ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:nn-tail-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:p1-n15-v ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-normal-r ;
    cd:narration "The upper-tail probability answers how often an individual result exceeds a chosen threshold. Under the stated stable-method model, about 2.275% of results exceed 10.20 mg/L. This frequency describes expected model behaviour."@en .
  ex:rv-n16 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-normal ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:normal-measurement-model ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:nn-ecdf-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n16-r ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n16-v ;
    cd:narration "The empirical CDF gives the observed fraction at or below each threshold. Using the same simulated sequence, the fraction at 10.20 mg/L is 0.978 for 1,000 results. The theoretical CDF supplies the corresponding population-model probability."@en .
  ex:rv-n16-r rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:CodeRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:optionalCode "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:hasCodeExample" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:nn-ecdf-code .
  ex:rv-n16-v rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:p1-ecdf-start .
  ex:rv-n17 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-normal ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:normal-measurement-model ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:nn-decision-f ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:nn-decision-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:p1-n17-v ;
    cd:narration "A quantile reverses the probability question. To leave 1% of individual results above the threshold, choose the 99th percentile: 10.232634787 mg/L for this known-parameter model. Repeated monitoring and estimated parameters require their own calibration."@en .
  ex:rv-n22 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-lognormal ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:lognormal-concentration-model ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-saved-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-saved-v ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n22-r ;
    cd:narration "These constructed datasets compare repeat injections with independent full preparations. Their histograms illustrate two possible patterns: roughly symmetric absolute variation and a right-skewed pattern consistent with relative effects. The sampling design determines which sources of variability each dataset includes."@en .
  ex:rv-n22-r rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:CodeRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:optionalCode "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:hasCodeExample" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:lg-compare-code .
  ex:rv-n25 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-lognormal ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:lognormal-concentration-model ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-definition-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-log-v ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n25-f ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n25-r ;
    cd:narration "A normally distributed log ratio produces a Lognormal concentration after exponentiation. The concentration stays positive and has a right tail. Increasing log SD while holding the median fixed widens that tail and raises the arithmetic expectation; the log-scale distribution remains symmetric."@en .
  ex:rv-n25-f rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:lg-definition .
  ex:rv-n25-r rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:CodeRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:optionalCode "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:position "4"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:hasCodeExample" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:lg-transform-code .
  ex:rv-n28 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-lognormal ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:lognormal-concentration-model ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-tail-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:p1-n28-v ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n28-f ;
    cd:narration "At log SD 0.30, the probability of exceeding 15 ng/L is about 0.08826. Reversing the question, a 5% upper-tail probability gives a threshold of about 16.38 ng/L. Both calculations use the Normal log-scale model and return to concentration units by exponentiation."@en .
  ex:rv-n28-f rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:lg-quantile .
  ex:rv-n29 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-lognormal ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:lognormal-concentration-model ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:lg-checks-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n29-c ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n29-r ;
    cd:narration "Model choice starts with the sampling unit: repeated preparation of one homogeneous sample describes repeatability; sampling different sites includes environmental variation. Mixtures, reporting limits and censoring can change the observed shape. Arithmetic and geometric summaries answer different reporting questions."@en .
  ex:rv-n29-c rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:DefinitionListRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:hasDefinitionListEntry" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:p1-population-cards .
  ex:rv-n29-r rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:CodeRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:optionalCode "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:hasCodeExample" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:lg-environment-code .
  ex:rv-n31 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-chi ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:al-chi-square ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:ic-question-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n31-v ;
    cd:narration "A new constructed nitrate QC series contains six independent readings. We compare its repeatability with a known reference SD of 0.10 mg/L, assuming Normal measurement results. The prespecified question is whether spread has increased, using a one-sided 5% level. An estimated reference SD would require a different comparison."@en .
  ex:rv-n31-v rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:ic-process-media .
  ex:rv-n32 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-chi ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:al-chi-square ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:ic-deviations-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:ic-deviations-t ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n32-f ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:ic-spread-answer-item ;
    cd:narration "Subtract the sample mean, 10.05 mg/L, from each QC result. The squared residuals sum to 0.12 (mg/L) squared. Dividing by five gives sample variance 0.024 (mg/L) squared; its positive square root gives sample SD about 0.155 mg/L."@en .
  ex:rv-n32-f rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:ic-spread .
  ex:ic-spread-answer-item rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "4"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:ic-spread-answer .
  ex:ic-spread-answer rdf:type cd:Interpretation ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:bodyFormat "markdown" ;
    cd:body "**The sample SD is about 0.155 mg/L, roughly 55% above the known reference SD of 0.10 mg/L.** The table supplies the squared deviations; dividing their sum by five gives the sample variance. A repeated-sampling model assesses how unusual this increase is under the reference method."@en .
  ex:rv-n34 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-chi ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:al-chi-square ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:ic-repeated-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-variance-r ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-variance-v ;
    cd:narration "Repeating a six-reading experiment produces a different estimated variance each time, even with fixed true SD. The histogram shows this sampling variability. The separately marked QC variance is 0.024 (mg/L) squared. A chi-square model describes the scaled variance under independent Normal sampling."@en .
  ex:rv-n36 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-chi ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:al-chi-square ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:ix-sum-f ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:ix-sum-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n36-v ;
    cd:narration "Adding independent squared standard-normal variables gives a chi-square distribution. Its degrees of freedom count the independent terms. For a sample variance, estimating the mean uses one degree of freedom, leaving n - 1."@en .
  ex:rv-n36-v rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:p1-five-squares .
  ex:rv-n41 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-chi ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:al-chi-square ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:ix-size-f ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:ix-size-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:p1-n41-v ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-variance-r ;
    cd:narration "Increasing the number of readings per series from 6 to 30 reduces the relative SD of the variance estimate from 63.2% to 26.3%, with true precision fixed. Increasing the simulation count instead refines the displayed histogram. Q also depends on degrees of freedom, so compare like-for-like reference distributions."@en .
  ex:rv-n44 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-t ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:l5-student-t ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n44-c ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-student-v ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:tf-denominator-h ;
    cd:narration "Student's distribution describes a centred sample mean divided by its estimated standard error under independent Normal sampling. Small denominator estimates produce heavier tails than the standard Normal. The experiment starts with n = 2 readings, giving one degree of freedom."@en .
  ex:rv-n44-c rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:DefinitionListRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:hasDefinitionListEntry" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:tf-denominator .
  ex:rv-n46 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-t ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:l5-student-t ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:p1-n46-v ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n46-c ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:tf-df-live-h ;
    cd:narration "Student densities are symmetric around zero. With 3 degrees of freedom, their tails are heavier than with 29. As sample size grows, the estimated standard error stabilizes and the Student distribution approaches the standard Normal."@en .
  ex:rv-n46-c rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:rv-n46-info .
  ex:rv-n46-info rdf:type cd:Interpretation ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body """- **More measurements:** a more stable estimated denominator.
- **More degrees of freedom:** lighter tails, closer to the normal density.
- **Same center:** the distributions remain symmetric around zero."""@en ;
    cd:bodyFormat "markdown" .
  ex:rv-n49 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-f ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:l5-f-distribution ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:dist-devices-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n49-f ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n49-v ;
    cd:narration "Two constructed independent groups each contain six readings. A has mean 10.10 mg/L and sample SD 0.10 mg/L; B has mean 10.00 mg/L and sample SD 0.30 mg/L. Their sample-variance ratio B/A is 9. Repeated pairs show how such ratios vary."@en .
  ex:rv-n49-f rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:tf-ratio .
  ex:rv-n49-v rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:ChartRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:rx-devices .
  ex:rv-n50 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-f ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:l5-f-distribution ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-f-v ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:tf-f-live-h ;
    cd:narration "Even with equal true variances, independent samples give varying variance estimates and B/A ratios. Small denominator estimates create a long right tail. Under Normal sampling, the reference distribution is F; the two population means may differ."@en .
  ex:rv-n60 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-tests ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:rev-qq ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rev-qq-read-c ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rev-qq-read-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rev-qq-read-v ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n60-f ;
    cd:narration "A new pair of constructed five-reading samples illustrates a Q-Q plot. Ordered observations are compared with quantiles of a fixed Normal model: mean 10 mg/L, SD 0.50 mg/L. A follows the identity line; B bends. This is a visual compatibility check, with limited information from five points."@en .
  ex:rv-n60-f rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "4"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:rev-qq-formula .
  ex:rv-n61 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-tests ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:l5-kolmogorov-smirnov ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rev-ks-overlay-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n61-c ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n61-r ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n61-v ;
    cd:narration "The Kolmogorov-Smirnov distance is the largest vertical gap between empirical and model CDFs, checking both sides of each jump. For these five-reading samples, the exact two-sided 5% cutoff is 0.563275: A's 0.144578 lies below it; B's 0.725747 exceeds it. This calibration assumes the stated fixed CDF; fitting parameters changes the reference."@en .
  ex:rv-n61-c rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:DefinitionListRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:hasDefinitionListEntry" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:rv-n61-info .
  ex:rv-n61-decision rdf:type cd:DefinitionListEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "Fixed model: compare both distances with 0.563275"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "Fixed Normal model: mean 10 mg/L, SD 0.50 mg/L. For five independent continuous observations, the exact two-sided 5% cutoff is 0.563275. A: 0.144578 lies below it. B: 0.725747 exceeds it. Measure gaps on both sides of each ECDF jump."@en ;
    cd:position "1"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:rv-n61-fitted rdf:type cd:DefinitionListEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "A model fitted to these data needs another reference"@en ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:body "Estimating mean and SD from the same observations changes the reference distribution. Use a suitable Lilliefors calibration or a parametric bootstrap that refits every replicate. Ties, censoring and dependence also need a matching calibration."@en ;
    cd:position "2"^^xsd:integer .
  ex:rv-n61-info rdf:type cd:DefinitionList ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:rv-n61-decision ;
    cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:rv-n61-fitted .
  ex:rv-n61-r rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:CodeRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:optionalCode "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:position "5"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:hasCodeExample" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:rev-ks-code .
  ex:rv-n61-v rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:rev-ks-media .
  ex:rv-n62 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-tests ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:l5-pearson-gof ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rev-pearson-start-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n62-f ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-pearson-v ;
    cd:narration "A separate particle-count example classifies 100 observations into five exhaustive categories with fixed probabilities. Expected counts are 10, 20, 40, 20, 10; observed counts are 4, 12, 44, 24, 16. The weighted squared discrepancies sum to 11.6. Their large-sample reference is approximately chi-square."@en .
  ex:rv-n62-f rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:position "3"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:l5-p20a-formula .
  ex:rv-n63 dct:subject ex:l5-topic-tests ;
    rdf:type cd:SceneDefinition ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:focusConcept ex:l5-pearson-gof ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:p1-n63-v ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rev-pearson-table-h ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:rv-n63-r ;
    cd:hasSceneItem ex:v3-n63-f ;
    cd:narration "The first Pearson contribution is (4 - 10) squared / 10 = 3.6. All five contributions sum to 11.6. With fixed category probabilities and a fixed total, the reference has four degrees of freedom.\n\nThe 5% cutoff is 9.487729 and p = 0.020587. The alternative compatible counts give statistic 0.225. This comparison assesses model compatibility; explaining a discrepancy requires further investigation."@en .
  ex:rv-n63-r rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
    cd:authoredResource "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:communicativeRole cd:CodeRole ;
    cd:language "en" ;
    cd:optionalCode "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    cd:position "4"^^xsd:integer ;
    cd:selectionPath "cd:hasCodeExample" ;
    cd:selectsResource ex:rev-pearson-code .
  ex:rv-normal-r rdf:type cd:SceneItem ;
